# Unicode CLDR 47, cldr-json cldr-dates-full/main/sw/dateFields.json.  "saa
# {0} iliyopita" / "saa {0} zilizopita" / "baada ya saa {0}" -- class 9/10,
# invariant for number.
#
# saa is a DURATION here and only a duration.  The same word names the hour of
# the day, and that reading is deliberately not shipped: Swahili's traditional
# clock counts the hours from sunrise, so "saa tatu" is 09:00 to one writer and
# 03:00 to another, and nothing in the phrase says which.  See
# test/nl_corpus_sw/test_sw_refusals.py for the pinned refusal, and lang.json
# for the clock grammar that admits the digital literal only.
saa
